blank\">here</a>. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T01:24:38-08:00","id":813987,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys. That brings us to three interested players, which would probably work quite well. Three is a good minimum, I think.<br /> <br /> We have a city flooded with new dead, Spanish Flu and the War both having played their part, with several nihils growing rather big as the spectre numbers also grow... In the midst of all this, of course, there's treason in Stygia and a big shake up of the Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The ghosts of the city would be primarily a combination of older Victorian dead (including those who died in the mills and workhouses, and those who died during the Peterloo Massacre), and newer war dead, jostling for a place in the bureaucracy of the afterlife. The city at that time was a melange of socialism and feminism, poverty and disease, industry and exploitation.<br /> <br /> I think some interesting stories could be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, s